/-!
# Fixtures for the official omega-Y expansion

Each fixture `(s, n, t)` says that the official program gives `s[n] = t`. The
official program is Naruyoko's StudyAndExpandSequence
(https://github.com/Naruyoko/StudyAndExpandSequence, commit `b26ba7e`, `expand`
with the default settings of v1.1). It was run as a black box; only its outputs
are recorded here.

The inputs are chosen so that every case of the rule (`notes/03-official-rule.md`
of koteitan/wy-wo-por, §2.4, cases 1 to 4) is used at region levels 2 to 5:

* `(1,3,3)`, `(1,4,4)`, `(1,4)`, `(1,4,6,4)`, `(1,3,4,3)`, and the three
  sequences of notes/03 §5 on which the weak rule differs from the official one;
* standard sequences from `reference/official/samples/` of wy-wo-por (S1, S2, S3, S6);
* legal sequences of length at most 5 with entries at most 7 (most are not
  standard).

Each input is expanded with `n = 1, 2, 3`. Only fixtures with official values
below `2^53` and at most 30 terms are used.

The checks are finite executable checks:

* (c) `Official.expand s n = t` for every fixture;
* (a) the mountain built by the expansion is the canonical mountain
  `Canonical.build t` (every row, value and stored left endpoint);
* (b) `t` is lexicographically smaller than `s`.

They are not a proof of anything about other inputs.
-/

